WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.255
This is a simplified teaching bus, not an exact E C E two twenty four protocol.

2
00:00:06.255 --> 00:00:09.940
The processor places an address on the address bus.

3
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.455
It then asserts a read request.

4
00:00:12.455 --> 00:00:17.550
The address identifies where to read; it is not the value being returned.

5
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.905
Keep the address stable while the memory responds.

6
00:00:20.905 --> 00:00:25.385
Memory drives the data bus and signals that the value is valid.

7
00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:29.755
The processor samples forty two only after that indication.

8
00:00:29.755 --> 00:00:35.220
In eight bits, forty two is zero zero one zero one zero one zero.

9
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.450
Sampling before data becomes valid can capture an old or unstable value.

10
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:45.360
Finally, the processor releases the request and the transaction ends.
